The container image built from the Dockerfile additionally bundles the following third-party
software, unmodified, each under its own license. Versions and SHA-256 pins are in
hack/images/checksums.txt (in the image: /usr/share/patrol-cd/tools.lock).

  - Helm 4.2.1 (https://github.com/helm/helm), Apache License 2.0. License text in the image:
    /usr/share/licenses/helm/LICENSE.
  - Kustomize 5.8.1 (https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kustomize), Apache License 2.0. License
    text in the image: /usr/share/licenses/kustomize/LICENSE.
  - git-lfs 3.7.1 (https://github.com/git-lfs/git-lfs), MIT License. License text in the image:
    /usr/share/licenses/git-lfs/LICENSE.md.
  - connect-proxy 1.106 (https://github.com/gotoh/ssh-connect), GPL-2.0-or-later, compiled from
    its single source file. /usr/share/licenses/connect-proxy/ in the image holds that source
    (connect.c), the text of the GNU General Public License version 2 (COPYING) and the compiler
    command used (BUILD); the binary is /usr/local/bin/connect-proxy. It runs as a separate
    process and Patrol CD does not link against it.
  - Alpine Linux packages: those of the alpine:3.24.2 base image, git, openssh-client, gpg,
    ca-certificates, tzdata, tini and their dependencies, each under the license its package
    declares. The image build does not copy their license texts into the image. Each installed
    package and its declared license are recorded in apk's package database, which stays in the
    image (/lib/apk/db/installed); the image SBOM (make image-sbom) also lists the packages.

